  "body": "## What\n\n`add_operation` refuses a 2D Contour whose `params` give a lead shape that is different from the seeded shape. The message does not name the cause.\n\nFound during the work on #2859 (example case `2d/contour-tabs`). Part of #2392.\n\n## Steps\n\nRun this script with `camcraft-cli script` on `upstream/main` 5fdbed9bd. A stock, a model and the tool `EM-0600-4FL` are in the document.\n\n```js\ncam.call(\"add_operation\", {\n  kind: \"2D Contour\",\n  tool: \"EM-0600-4FL\",\n  source: \"contour-tabs\",\n  params: { lead: { arc: { radius: 3.0 } } }\n});\n```\n\n## Result\n\n```\ncamcraft-cli: call: add_operation: bad params patch: invalid value: map, expected map with a single key\n```\n\n## Cause (as read from the behaviour)\n\nThe tool applies `params` as a JSON merge patch on the seeded parameters. The seeded lead is `{ \"linear\": { \"length\": 8.0 } }`. The merged value has the two keys `linear` and `arc`. The lead is an enum with one key, so the parse fails.\n\n## Workaround\n\nRemove the seeded key in the same patch:\n\n```js\nparams: { lead: { linear: null, arc: { radius: 3.0 } } }\n```\n\n## Expected\n\nOne of these:\n\n- The patch replaces the lead when it names a different shape.\n- The refusal names the field and the cause, for example: `lead: give one shape only (found linear and arc)`.\n\nThe same merge applies to `edit_operation` and to each parameter that is an enum with data (`links.approach.lead_out` is one). The fix must cover them.\n\n## Done means\n\nA test in `crates/app/tests/` gives `lead: { arc: { radius: 3.0 } }` to `add_operation` and to `edit_operation` for a 2D Contour. The operation gets the arc lead, or the refusal names `lead` and the two shapes. The `camcraft-mcp` skill says how to change a lead shape.\n",
